<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<ids:ids xmlns:ids="http://standards.buildingsmart.org/IDS" xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://standards.buildingsmart.org/IDS http://standards.buildingsmart.org/IDS/1.0/ids.xsd">
  <!--edit with ONESTRUCTION Inc.-->
  <ids:info>
    <ids:title>BDNS two-way validation (IFC4X3_ADD2) - part-1</ids:title>
    <ids:copyright>ONESTRUCTION Inc.</ids:copyright>
    <ids:version>1.0.0</ids:version>
    <ids:description>Generated by ONESTRUCTION Inc. from the buildingSMART UK&amp;I / Open Data Institute BDNS Abbreviations Register (theodi/BDNS @ fb56a0982f4177eceda2fdcf2330d5efbcd4957c), 943 rows, column 'ifc4_3'. Each register row yields a forward specification (asset name -&gt; IFC entity, description and classification) and contributes to a reverse specification grouped by entity and PredefinedType (IFC entity -&gt; permitted asset codes). Declared schema IFC4X3_ADD2; occurrence names match CODE[type]-number per the BDNS_Specification_naming_syntax.md (Device/Asset role name) in tolerant mode (specification plus leading zeros and optional hyphen-delimited prefix and suffix, as found in practice); the abbreviation is also required as an IfcClassificationReference in system 'BDNS' per section 3.9.1; applicability cardinality optional. Entities and PredefinedTypes validated against the declared IFC schema with IfcOpenShell; rows not expressible in that schema are omitted rather than approximated. Contributors: Khalil.ib2111@gmail.com. This file covers part 1: 320 of the register's 943 rows.</ids:description>
    <ids:author>lucas@onestruction.com</ids:author>
    <ids:date>2026-07-29</ids:date>
    <ids:purpose>Two-way validation of BDNS asset codes against IFC entity classification</ids:purpose>
    <ids:milestone>Handover</ids:milestone>
  </ids:info>
  <ids:specifications>
